From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 01:30:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 61/68] hottyterm: scrolls and a finger's moves paint on the
 paint thread

A scroll (wheel, touchpad, touch drag) and a touch's move that pans a
surface no longer repaint on the thread that handed them over, GTK's
main thread. They mark the host dirty and wake the paint thread, which
repaints from the latest position. While a paint is under way, the
latest move and the sum of the scrolls since wait for it, rather than
the main thread waiting out the paint; the paint thread, or anyone else
who waits for the host, hands them over first, so a lift never goes
ahead of its moves. Such paints hold no renderer: no cells change with
them, and held paint after paint the renderer drew nothing.

GDK compresses pointer motion and smooth scrolls to one per frame, but
not a touch's updates. At a touchscreen's 120 Hz, a 6 ms repaint per
update kept the event queue from emptying, and the frame clock, which
runs once it has, showed nothing for up to a second during a drag.

All in src/termio/hotty.zig: no lines in upstream files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
